section: ghc-internal
synopsis:
  Fix a lock-up in the MIO I/O manager when the polling backend reports an error
description:
  An error reported by the MIO backends ``epoll`` or ``kqueue`` -- for instance ``EBADF`` after a
  file descriptor was closed concurrently -- could leave the IO manager in a
  state from which it never recovered: file descriptors could no longer be
  closed, and the threads doing so stopped responding to ``killThread`` and
  ``timeout``.  ``closeFdWith`` now restores its callback tables on every path
  and runs the fd's callbacks without an uninterruptible mask, ``closeFd_`` no
  longer abandons the close when the backend complains, ``selectCallbacks`` no
  longer takes the capability's ``EventManager`` down with it, and the cleanup
  of ``threadWait`` no longer replaces the asynchronous exception being
  delivered.
mrs: !16703
